{"title":"Conversions","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>conversion</b> is a special type of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ratio\" title=\"Ratio\">ratio</a> used to convert from one unit of measurement to another. These ratios are known as <b>conversion factors</b>.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Example\">Example</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Conversions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Example\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Suppose we wanted to know how many inches are in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> feet. Since we know there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> inches in a foot, our conversion factor is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/e/68e3c5ba286c189ff9dab165528ad171832c7eba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{12\\text{ inches}}{1\\text{ feet}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"70\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/5/535804ef899e336c1691af78dd75c9d5a60f25eb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3\\;\\cancel{\\text{feet}}\\cdot\\frac{12\\text{ inches}}{1\\;\\cancel{\\text{feet}}}=\\boxed{36\\;\\text{inches}}\\]\" width=\"227\" height=\"39\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> feet.\\\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Conversions&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018081559\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.014 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 25/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 274/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 976/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.800      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.800      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:19741:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018081559 and revision id 271476. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}